OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Tue 10 Nov to Thu 19 Nov
OL,6,FHigh pressure begins to migrate away
OL,7,Fto the east allowing frontal systems
OL,8,Fto progress into the UK from the
OL,9,Fsouthwest, although exactly how much
OL,10,Fprogress into the UK this makes is
OL,11,Funcertain. However there is a greater
OL,12,Fchance that at least the southern half
OL,13,Fof the UK will see a change to milder
OL,14,Fand wetter conditions, at least for a
OL,15,Ftime, while the north is more likely
OL,16,Fto remain drier. Toward the end of
OL,17,Fnext week we may start to see some
OL,18,Fcolder conditions spread from the
OL,19,Fnorth. While the nature of this colder
OL,20,Foutbreak is very uncertain, it could
OL,21,Fbring some wintry showers to the
OL,22,Fnorthern UK briefly. Thereafter, a
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Ftransition towards a westerly flow is
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Flikely, bringing changeable conditions
OL,25,Fwith rain more likely focused towards
OL,26,Fthe north west.
